      "note": "Drawn once a track off its own stream (none 45, a shaken top 30 in two patterns, a rim answer 15 in two, a hand exchange 10 in two: the manual's P1-P4 prior, each family split among its patterns). It enters only where a phrase's plan says (support-change), in a full passage, for one or two phrases, and every entry has its exit; then it rests at least a phrase. Each part sits apart from the hats: the shaken top on the odd sixteenths the hats leave, an alternating accent with weaker strokes between; the rim one dry answer in the gap after the loud backbeat; the hands a call in one bar and its answer two bars later, most bars resting. Never the old sixteenths: at most a third of a cycle's steps."
